Trama experimental Flatpak
=========================
Trama code and supplied artwork: GPL-3.0-only. See trama/LICENSE.
The supplied icon, mascot and hero were generated with ChatGPT and provided by
the project owner. No human authorship or exclusivity is claimed.
The new AppStream metadata document alone is CC0-1.0; this does not change the
license of the application, artwork or dependencies.

GPU Screen Recorder 6.1.7: GPL-3.0-only, commit
f97d1e392816503282d20a0804c3ce3fd2943767. See gsr/LICENSE.
https://git.dec05eba.com/gpu-screen-recorder/
Packaging replaces the upstream Flatpak ID and uses an unprivileged launcher
for per-session Polkit authorization. No GSR graphical application is included.

FFmpeg 9.0 is built statically using GSR's build scripts, configuration and
original patches (NVENC runtime negotiation and mbedTLS default CA certificates).
The enabled GPL/version3 configuration is governed by GPL version 3 or later;
component-specific notices and exceptions remain in the source. See ffmpeg/.
It links x264, Opus, LAME, mbedTLS and SRT, with their original notices retained.
NV codec headers are a build input, not an NVIDIA driver bundled with Trama.
libdrm is linked into the KMS helper. The i965 VAAPI driver is also bundled.
See the component notice folders and the companion source archive for original
licenses, copyright statements, patches and build instructions.

Rust dependency license declarations and original license/notice files are in
rust/. The inventory includes vendored build-time/other-target dependencies.
zune-core and zune-jpeg omit standalone license files; their manifest and source
header declarations are retained together with the Apache-2.0 license text.

The Flatpak runtime and graphics extensions supply shared libraries/tools and
retain their own licenses. The static helper also contains SDK libc/libgcc code;
see sdk/ and the source archive's SDK provenance and outstanding source checklist.
Do not describe this package as wholly GPL code or as a strong security sandbox.
